      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In light of the new threat assessment indicating a 35% probability of service disruption, we are revising our approach. Our revised strategy for the handover to the new Sovereign-Local LLM framework will involve increased shadow-running time to establish robust load balancing prior to decommissioning core modules. We will continue to prioritize seven-day cycles for real-time insights into national liquidity buffers, especially sensitivity to tax-related variabilities. Moreover, our revised timeline will account for potentially extended phases in interconnected sectors like municipal banking to ensure digital continuity for our citizens. All stakeholders, including your team, will be looped in for real-time updates to mitigate the risks and keep the transition as smooth as possible. Efforts will be taken to avoid catastrophic service downtimes during the critical period just before the 48-hour module decommissioning.",
